RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
October 4, 2010
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne convened in regular session beginning at 12:00
p.m. in Council Chambers for the purpose of acting upon vouchers for payment as presented.
Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen; COUNCIL MEMBERS - Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles,
Ms. Case, Dr. Rinne, Mr. Spiker and Mr. Valdez.  Absent: Ms. Ash, Mr. Collins and Mr. Pierson.
Also present:  Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, and John Knepper, Staff
Attorney.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.
Mr. Spiker moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr. Valdez.
Mr. Brown declared a conflict of interest (business interest in voucher payable to Ameri-Tech
HVAC Services, $30,437.50) and vacated Council Chambers for the remainder of the meeting.
Upon inquiry, Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, provided information relative to the voucher payable to
Ameri-Tech HVAC Services specific to budget fund #001-21-2111, stating the fund is a general
maintenance account line item used to cover many City building areas.  Motion to approve carried.
Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present in Council Chambers.
Purpose of the meeting having been met, Mayor Kaysen adjourned the meeting at 12:03 p.m.
Submitted by,
Carol Intlekofer, MMC
City Clerk
This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request
Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle
October 8, 2010
```
